* ORD (character -> ordinal value, the inverse of CHAR) is unimplemented in scrip: fatal parse-
* time "Error 5 -- Undefined function or operation", no output at all (root cause of
* csnobol4_suite/ord.sno's RC1).  sbl -bf ALSO refuses it (runtime ERROR 022 -- undefined
* function called) though it degrades softer (continues to a stats dump, rc=0) rather than
* refusing to compile.  Both tools lack ORD -- likely a CSNOBOL4-only extension outside SCRIP's
* stated SPITBOL-semantics target, not a confirmed SCRIP-specific gap.
	OUTPUT = ORD('A')
END
